  "Welcome back to The Sound Above. I am Mike Hall. Today we enter Philosophy, Empathy & Craftsmanship. Before code synthesis models and automated agents, developers met face to face to establish standards of craftsmanship. Today we rewatch Episode 22: Coraline Ada Ehmke from RailsConf 2014 (2014).",
  "Coraline was a Chicago developer, writer, and speaker active in local user groups, arguing that technical craftsmanship cannot be separated from interpersonal ethics.",
  "What led Coraline Ada Ehmke to author the Contributor Covenant? How did early Chicago software craft debates connect to ethical open-source governance? What principles guided Coraline Ada Ehmke when this conversation was recorded? How do those lessons inform the software systems we design today?",
